/**
 * Upstream Mermaid 12.3.0's drawing of a `block-beta` whose author wrote a fetching `classDef`,
 * for the sanitizer row of `tests/mermaid-svg.test.ts` that reads a kept `<style>`.
 *
 * Source:
 *
 *     block-beta
 *       columns 2
 *       a["Dispatch"] b["Drawn"]
 *       a --> b
 *       classDef evil fill:#ff0000,mask-image:url(https://evil.example/m.png),marker-end:url(#dispatch-mermaid-0_block-pointEnd)
 *       class a evil
 *
 * `block-beta` is a type beautiful-mermaid has no layout for, so a reader's source of it is
 * drawn by Mermaid, and Mermaid writes an author's `classDef` into the drawing's own `<style>`
 * (`createCssStyles`) as well as into the node's `style` attribute. The `marker-end` names a
 * marker of this very drawing, so the row reads a local `url(#id)` surviving in the sheet beside
 * the remote one that goes.
 *
 * Recorded by rendering that source through
 * `packages/dispatch/web/src/features/refs/mermaid-upstream.ts` under Bun -- so under the
 * configuration that module's `initialize` sets (theme `base` with Dispatch's palette,
 * `securityLevel: "strict"`, `htmlLabels: false`, `deterministicIds: true`,
 * `suppressErrorRendering: true`) and against that module's own DOM shim -- with one stub on
 * `globalThis` the shim needs and Bun has not:
 *
 *     class OffscreenCanvas {
 *       constructor(width, height) {}
 *       getContext(kind) {
 *         return kind === "2d"
 *           ? { font: "", measureText: (text) => ({ width: text.length * 8 }) }
 *           : null;
 *       }
 *     }
 *
 * Every length below was measured through that `measureText`, so a different width per character
 * records a different drawing. One source per process, so the render id is `dispatch-mermaid-0`,
 * which is what the sheet's own selectors and the marker the `classDef` names are written from.
 *
 * This drawing is committed whole, its `<style>` included, which is what the row reads; the two
 * fixtures beside it have theirs taken out. Its labels are SVG `<text>`, so it holds no
 * `foreignObject` and no void tag, and the row reads it with the XML parser, under which
 * happy-dom keeps an svg `<style>`'s text. The whole drawing under the parse the page uses for
 * Mermaid's markup is read by a browser row instead (`packages/dispatch/e2e/mermaid.e2e.ts`).
 */
